&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Postscript is the AI messaging platform trusted by 20,000+ Shopify brands — including Brooklinen, Ruggable, True Classic, and Dr. Squatch.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a mission to make SMS your number one revenue driving channel, we built the best-in-class SMS marketing platform and launched revenue-driving AI features not available on any other platform. And we&#39;re just getting started.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by Greylock and Y Combinator, fully remote since 2018.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; at Postscript, you&#39;ll be a high-ownership contributor to one of our core product or platform teams — owning meaningful systems end-to-end, driving technical quality, and helping shape how we build across the organization. Our engineering teams operate at the intersection of scale and product velocity, which means you&#39;ll be working on distributed systems that matter to the business while also influencing the technical standards that allow Postscript to grow sustainably.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-autonomy role for engineers who are energized by ambiguity, take genuine ownership of their work, and bring a strong point of view on how to build things well — without sacrificing speed or pragmatism. AI isn&#39;t a nice-to-have here — it&#39;s central to how we work. We expect our engineers to be active practitioners of AI-first development: fluent with the latest agentic coding tools, curious about what&#39;s emerging, and constantly pushing the boundary of what&#39;s possible with AI in their day-to-day craft. If you&#39;re the kind of engineer who&#39;s already experimenting with new models and tooling before anyone asks you to, you&#39;ll feel at home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior engineer at Postscript, you’ll no longer be only writing code but orchestrating it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is fully remote and can be based in the US or Canada.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take deep ownership of systems and product areas on your team — becoming the go-to technical expert for what you own&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently investigate, design, and execute solutions across distributed systems with a high degree of ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, build, and maintain highly available, scalable REST APIs and backend services for internal and external use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive system decoupling, modularization, and technical debt reduction — improving long-term maintainability without blocking near-term delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build agentically as your default: leveraging concurrent autonomous agent workflows, owning the output, and keeping a steady queue of aligned work moving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay at the forefront of emerging AI tooling and practices, bringing new techniques back to the team and helping raise the floor for how Postscript engineers work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to how we think about integrating AI into our systems and workflows — not just using AI tools, but helping shape where and how AI creates leverage across the engineering org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with product, data, and go-to-market teams — communicating clearly and proactively in an async-first environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and eliminate single points of failure, improving system resilience and knowledge redundancy across your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve how engineering gets done: bring better tools, fix workflow friction, build internal utilities when the leverage compounds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;ll Love About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience building large-scale backend systems and APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an active, daily user of AI coding tools and are using them to maximize your output — Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, or equivalent — and can speak concretely to how they&#39;ve changed your output and your workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech stack: Python, Go, React, and TypeScript; experience with Kubernetes, AWS, Datadog, and relational/NoSQL databases. You run agentic workflows autonomously and concurrently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You follow the AI tooling landscape closely: new model releases, emerging agentic workflows, and evolving best practices aren&#39;t things you catch up on eventually — they&#39;re things you&#39;re tracking in real time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think critically about AI output — you know where it accelerates you, where it introduces risk, and how to verify what it produces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to context switch extremely quickly across concurrent workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on both 0-to-1 initiatives and complex existing systems — and knowing how to balance building new things with improving what&#39;s there&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of relational and NoSQL databases, SQL, and thoughtful database modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity building and observing applications on AWS, and ideally with Datadog or comparable observability tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, direct communication — cross-functional partners and async teams can count on you to surface information proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong instincts for technical tradeoffs informed by both engineering best practices and business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Love About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary range of USD $175,000–$205,000 base plus significant equity (we do not have geo-based salaries)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High growth startup — plenty of room for you to directly impact the company and grow your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from home (or wherever in US / Canada)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fun — we&#39;re passionate and enjoy what we do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and opportunity for equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health, dental, vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For information about how we use your personal data, please see our U.S. Job Applicant&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://postscript.io/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://postscript.io/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;You are welcome here. Postscript is an ever-evolving place of equal employment for talented individuals.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
